<title>SWITZERLAND: Memphis top world air cargo airport in July - ACI.</title>
<headline>Memphis top world air cargo airport in July - ACI.</headline>
<dateline>GENEVA 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Memphis, base of U.S. express freight carrier, Federal Express, was the world's busiest cargo airport in July 1996, said Geneva-based Airports Council International (ACI).</p>
<p>The airport handled 167,174 tonnes of cargo in the month in question, up 26.9 percent on July 1995.</p>
<p>Occupying second-place in the ACI table of top cargo-airports was Los Angeles which handled 140,503 tonnes, up 9.7 percent on the previous year's levels.</p>
<p>In third place was Miami with 137,515 tonnes, an increase of 15.0 percent on July 1995.</p>
<p>The world's 20 busiest cargo airports in July this year, (July 1995) with individual volumes and percentage change over July 1995 are:</p>
<p>	  City		Tonnes	     Pct change from</p>
<p>						     a year ago</p>
<p> 1 (3)   Memphis	  167,174 tonnes   up  26.9pct</p>
<p> 2 (5)   Los Angeles    140,503 tonnes   up   9.7</p>
<p> 3 (7)   Miami	    137,515 tonnes   up  15.0</p>
<p> 4 (1)   Tokyo	    135,264 tonnes   down 5.3</p>
<p> 5 (2)   New York	 134,820 tonnes   up   0.1</p>
<p> 6 (4)   Hong Kong	133,700 tonnes   up   1.9</p>
<p> 7 (6)   Frankfurt	123,111 tonnes   up   1.0</p>
<p> 8 (9)   Seoul	    112,047 tonnes   up  10.8</p>
<p> 9 (8)   Louisville     110,686 tonnes   up   8.2</p>
<p> 10(13)  Anchorage	104,146 tonnes   up  15.1</p>
<p> 11(10)  Chicago	  103,774 tonnes   up   4.3</p>
<p> 12(11)  Singapore	 99,024 tonnes   up   2.3</p>
<p> 13(12)  Heathrow	  94,842 tonnes   down 0.2</p>
<p> 14(15)  Paris-CDG	 84,323 tonnes   up   6.7</p>
<p> 15(14)  Amsterdam	 83,599 tonnes   up   2.6</p>
<p> 16(16)  New York Newark 80,767 tonnes   up   2.7</p>
<p> 17(19)  Atlanta	   66,106 tonnes   up  12.9</p>
<p> 18(17)  Taipei	    63,748 tonnes   down 0.5</p>
<p> 19 (-)  Dallas F/W	60,903 tonnes   up   5.2</p>
<p> 20 (-)  Haneda	    59,453 tonnes   up  19.8</p>
